      "text": [
        "560 - وَ سُئِلَ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ: عَنْ قَوْلِ اَللَّهِ عَزَّ وَ جَلَّ: «۝ أَوَلَمْ يَرَوْا۟ أَنَّا نَأْتِى ٱلْأَرْضَ نَنقُصُهَا مِنْ أَطْرَافِهَا ۚ وَٱللَّهُ يَحْكُمُ لَا مُعَقِّبَ لِحُكْمِهِۦ ۚ وَهُوَ سَرِيعُ ٱلْحِسَابِ ۝»\nفَقَالَ «فَقْدُ اَلْعُلَمَاءِ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.560 - Imam Jafar ibn Muhammad Al-Sadiq (as) was asked about the meaning of Allah’s (swt) words:\n\"Do they not see that We are advancing upon the land, reducing it from its borders? And Allah (swt) judges; there is no adjuster of His ruling, and He is swift in account.\" (Surah Ar-Ra’d 13:41).\nImam (as) replied: \"The loss of the scholars.\""
        ]
      }
